1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,010
Mini Drone Parcel Route.

2
00:00:02,060 --> 00:00:08,850
An AI Fundamentals final project at QAIRU
by Akhmetzhan Turlybek.

3
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:14,770
A drone needs to deliver one parcel across
a six-by-six map.

4
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:19,050
It has to get around obstacles and decide
whether to take off.

5
00:00:19,320 --> 00:00:24,110
Before it flies, a weather sensor gives it
one clue about the wind.

6
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:30,610
A-star finds the shortest route.

7
00:00:30,860 --> 00:00:34,890
It adds the steps taken so far to the
Manhattan distance remaining.

8
00:00:35,060 --> 00:00:38,810
That distance counts the rows and columns
still to cross.

9
00:00:39,160 --> 00:00:41,710
The shortest route takes ten steps.

10
00:00:41,980 --> 00:00:45,190
A-star expands eleven nodes with this
estimate.

11
00:00:45,580 --> 00:00:49,530
With the estimate set to zero, the search
expands thirty-three.

12
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:52,030
The route length stays the same.

13
00:00:55,500 --> 00:00:59,770
Before the alert, the probability of wind
is zero point three zero.

14
00:01:00,400 --> 00:01:07,850
The sensor alerts with probability zero
point eight zero when it’s windy, and zero
point two zero when it’s calm.

15
00:01:08,320 --> 00:01:14,230
Once the alert comes in, Bayes’ rule
raises our wind belief to zero point six
three one six.

16
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:22,990
One Bellman update combines the route and
the wind belief.

17
00:01:23,320 --> 00:01:27,870
Flying earns ten in calm weather and loses
twenty in wind.

18
00:01:28,120 --> 00:01:33,830
Weighting those rewards by their
probabilities gives Fly a score of minus
eight point nine five.

19
00:01:34,500 --> 00:01:36,270
Wait scores minus two.

20
00:01:36,320 --> 00:01:38,850
That’s higher, so the drone waits.

21
00:01:43,500 --> 00:01:45,090
Now we turn off the alert.

22
00:01:45,140 --> 00:01:51,150
The route stays at ten steps, but the wind
belief falls to zero point zero nine six
eight.

23
00:01:51,580 --> 00:01:55,470
That’s below the break-even probability of
zero point four zero.

24
00:01:55,740 --> 00:01:57,830
The decision flips to Fly.

25
00:02:02,500 --> 00:02:04,750
Both approaches to the goal are blocked.

26
00:02:04,860 --> 00:02:09,110
A-star finds no route, so the app selects
Wait.

27
00:02:09,320 --> 00:02:12,270
The drone needs a route before it can take
off.

28
00:02:15,500 --> 00:02:16,790
All tests pass.

29
00:02:16,900 --> 00:02:21,510
They cover both alert settings, the longer
route, and the blocked goal.

30
00:02:21,560 --> 00:02:24,630
The two searches also agree on route
length.

31
00:02:25,500 --> 00:02:27,430
The code is available on GitHub.
